  "facts": [
    "The Arlberg Road Tunnel, Austria's longest at 13.976 kilometres, opened in 1978 as the world's longest road tunnel, stretching beneath the Arlberg massif between Tyrol and Vorarlberg.",
    "Built between July 1974 and December 1978, the tunnel cost 4 billion Austrian schillings (~€300 million) and features a 736‑metre shaft, the deepest in Europe, plus 12 vents and 43 traffic cameras.",
    "In 2015, Asfinag added Vehicle Hotspot Detectors at both mouths, banning trucks over 3.5 t with overheated engines, brakes, or exhausts from using the tunnel to ensure safety."
